---
import { translations, type SupportedLocale } from '../i18n/translations';

interface Props {
  lang?: SupportedLocale;
}

const { lang = 'en' } = Astro.props;
const t = translations[lang] || translations.en;
---

<section class="w-full max-w-5xl mx-auto px-3 sm:px-6 py-10 sm:py-16 border-t border-white/[0.08]" aria-labelledby="beginner-guide-heading">
  
  <!-- Section Title -->
  <div class="text-center max-w-2xl mx-auto mb-10 sm:mb-12">
    <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3.5 py-1.5 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold bg-emerald-500/15 border border-emerald-400/30 text-emerald-300 mb-3 animate-shimmer">
      <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5 text-emerald-300 shrink-0" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
        <path d="M11 20A7 7 0 0 1 9.8 6.1C15.5 5 17 4.48 19 2c1 2 2 4.18 2 8 0 5.5-4.78 10-10 10Z"/>
        <path d="M2 21c0-3 1.85-5.36 5.08-6C9.5 14.52 12 13 13 12"/>
      </svg>
      <span>New to Meditation? Start Here</span>
    </div>
    <h2 id="beginner-guide-heading" class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white">
      Meditation Made Simple: A Beginner's 3-Step Guide
    </h2>
    <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-zinc-400 mt-2 max-w-lg mx-auto leading-relaxed">
      No chanting, no expensive subscriptions, and no complicated rules. Just you, your breath, and a moment of genuine stillness.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- 3 Simple Steps Grid -->
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 sm:gap-6 mb-12 sm:mb-16">
    
    <!-- Step 1 -->
    <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl sm:rounded-3xl bg-white/[0.02] border border-white/[0.06] hover:border-emerald-400/30 transition-all flex flex-col justify-between">
      <div>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-4">
          <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-emerald-500/15 border border-emerald-400/30 text-emerald-300 font-bold text-sm flex items-center justify-center">
            1
          </span>
          <div class="w-9 h-9 rounded-xl bg-emerald-500/10 border border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center justify-center">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-emerald-400" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
              <path d="M19 9V6a2 2 0 0 0-2-2H7a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v3"/>
              <path d="M3 16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h14a2 2 0 0 0 2-2v-5a2 2 0 0 0-2-2H5a2 2 0 0 0-2 2Z"/>
              <path d="M6 18v3"/>
              <path d="M18 18v3"/>
            </svg>
          </div>
        </div>
        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-white mb-2">
          Sit Comfortably
        </h3>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
          You don't need to sit cross-legged on the floor. An ordinary chair, couch, or bed works great. Keep your back comfortably straight, rest your hands on your lap, and soften your shoulders.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-4 pt-3 border-t border-white/[0.04] text-[11px] text-emerald-400/90 font-medium">
        Tip: Keep your posture relaxed yet alert.
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Step 2 -->
    <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl sm:rounded-3xl bg-white/[0.02] border border-white/[0.06] hover:border-cyan-400/30 transition-all flex flex-col justify-between">
      <div>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-4">
          <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-cyan-500/15 border border-cyan-400/30 text-cyan-300 font-bold text-sm flex items-center justify-center">
            2
          </span>
          <div class="w-9 h-9 rounded-xl bg-cyan-500/10 border border-cyan-500/20 flex items-center justify-center">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-cyan-400" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
              <path d="M17.7 7.7a2.5 2.5 0 1 1 1.8 4.3H2"/>
              <path d="M9.6 4.6A2 2 0 1 1 11 8H2"/>
              <path d="M12.6 19.4A2 2 0 1 0 14 16H2"/>
            </svg>
          </div>
        </div>
        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-white mb-2">
          Follow Your Natural Breath
        </h3>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
          Gently close your eyes or gaze softly downward. Do not try to force or control your breathing. Simply pay attention to where you feel it most—the cool air at your nostrils, or your belly gently rising and falling.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-4 pt-3 border-t border-white/[0.04] text-[11px] text-cyan-400/90 font-medium">
        Tip: Your breath is your home anchor.
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Step 3 -->
    <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl sm:rounded-3xl bg-white/[0.02] border border-white/[0.06] hover:border-purple-400/30 transition-all flex flex-col justify-between">
      <div>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-4">
          <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-purple-500/15 border border-purple-400/30 text-purple-300 font-bold text-sm flex items-center justify-center">
            3
          </span>
          <div class="w-9 h-9 rounded-xl bg-purple-500/10 border border-purple-500/20 flex items-center justify-center">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-purple-400" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
              <path d="M3 12a9 9 0 1 0 9-9 9.75 9.75 0 0 0-6.74 2.74L3 8"/>
              <path d="M3 3v5h5"/>
            </svg>
          </div>
        </div>
        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-white mb-2">
          When Thoughts Pop Up, Return
        </h3>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
          Here is the biggest secret: <strong class="text-white">your mind will wander</strong>, and that is 100% normal! The second you notice you're daydreaming, don't get frustrated. Simply notice it, smile, and gently return to your next breath.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-4 pt-3 border-t border-white/[0.04] text-[11px] text-purple-400/90 font-medium">
        Tip: Noticing mind-wandering IS the practice.
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>

  <!-- 4 Golden Rules for New Meditators -->
  <div class="rounded-2xl sm:rounded-3xl bg-white/[0.02] border border-white/[0.06] p-5 sm:p-8 md:p-10 mb-12 sm:mb-16">
    <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto text-center mb-8">
      <h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white">
        4 Golden Rules Every Beginner Should Know
      </h3>
      <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-zinc-400 mt-1.5">
        Relieve the pressure and make your mindfulness habit effortless.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
      
      <div class="p-4 sm:p-5 rounded-2xl bg-white/[0.02] border border-white/[0.04]">
        <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-xl bg-cyan-500/10 border border-cyan-500/20 text-cyan-400 flex items-center justify-center mb-2.5">
          <svg class="w-4 h-4" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><polyline points="12 6 12 12 16 14"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h4 class="text-sm font-semibold text-white mb-1">1. Start with Just 3 to 5 Minutes</h4>
        <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
          Never feel pressured to sit for 30 or 60 minutes right away. A 3-minute or 5-minute session done consistently every morning builds more neuroplastic strength than a sporadic hour once a month.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-4 sm:p-5 rounded-2xl bg-white/[0.02] border border-white/[0.04]">
        <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-xl bg-emerald-500/10 border border-emerald-500/20 text-emerald-400 flex items-center justify-center mb-2.5">
          <svg class="w-4 h-4" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h4 class="text-sm font-semibold text-white mb-1">2. There is No Such Thing as a "Bad" Session</h4>
        <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
          If your mind feels busy, restless, or loud today, you didn't fail. A workout where the weights felt heavy is still a workout. Showing up and hearing the closing bell is your victory.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-4 sm:p-5 rounded-2xl bg-white/[0.02] border border-white/[0.04]">
        <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-xl bg-purple-500/10 border border-purple-500/20 text-purple-400 flex items-center justify-center mb-2.5">
          <svg class="w-4 h-4" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="5" r="3"/><line x1="12" y1="22" x2="12" y2="8"/><path d="M5 12H2a10 10 0 0 0 20 0h-3"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h4 class="text-sm font-semibold text-white mb-1">3. Anchor It to an Existing Habit</h4>
        <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
          The easiest way to remember to meditate is habit-stacking. Meditate right after brewing your morning tea, or right before turning off your computer for the evening.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-4 sm:p-5 rounded-2xl bg-white/[0.02] border border-white/[0.04]">
        <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-xl bg-amber-500/10 border border-amber-500/20 text-amber-400 flex items-center justify-center mb-2.5">
          <svg class="w-4 h-4" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 8a6 6 0 0 1 12 0c0 7 3 9 3 9H3s3-2 3-9"/><path d="M10.3 21a1.94 1.94 0 0 0 3.4 0"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h4 class="text-sm font-semibold text-white mb-1">4. Trust the Bell, Forget the Clock</h4>
        <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
          Avoid peeking at the screen. That's why our timer features resonant Tibetan bowls and screen wake lock—trust that the bell will chime when your session completes.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Beginner 30-Day Milestone Roadmap -->
  <div class="rounded-2xl sm:rounded-3xl bg-white/[0.02] border border-white/[0.06] p-5 sm:p-8 md:p-10 mb-12 sm:mb-16">
    <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto text-center mb-8">
      <h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white">
        Your First 30 Days: A Realistic Roadmap
      </h3>
      <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-zinc-400 mt-1">
        What to expect as your brain adapts to daily stillness.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-3 sm:gap-4">
      
      <div class="p-4 rounded-2xl bg-white/[0.03] border border-white/[0.06] relative">
        <div class="text-xs font-bold text-emerald-400 uppercase tracking-wider mb-1">Days 1–7</div>
        <h4 class="text-sm font-semibold text-white mb-2">The Spark (3–5 Mins)</h4>
        <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
          Your primary focus is simply showing up. You might feel restless or notice how active your mind is. This awareness is step one.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-4 rounded-2xl bg-white/[0.03] border border-white/[0.06] relative">
        <div class="text-xs font-bold text-cyan-400 uppercase tracking-wider mb-1">Days 8–14</div>
        <h4 class="text-sm font-semibold text-white mb-2">The Anchor (5–7 Mins)</h4>
        <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
          You begin noticing the gap between a stressful thought and your reaction. Returning to your breath starts feeling more natural and less effortful.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-4 rounded-2xl bg-white/[0.03] border border-white/[0.06] relative">
        <div class="text-xs font-bold text-blue-400 uppercase tracking-wider mb-1">Days 15–21</div>
        <h4 class="text-sm font-semibold text-white mb-2">The Calm Center (10 Mins)</h4>
        <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
          Physical relaxation deepens. You'll likely notice better sleep quality, improved patience in conversations, and lowered afternoon fatigue.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-4 rounded-2xl bg-white/[0.03] border border-white/[0.06] relative">
        <div class="text-xs font-bold text-purple-400 uppercase tracking-wider mb-1">Days 22–30+</div>
        <h4 class="text-sm font-semibold text-white mb-2">The Sanctuary (10–15 Mins)</h4>
        <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
          Meditation is no longer a chore on your to-do list; it becomes a tranquil refuge you look forward to every day.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Beginner Myth-Busters & FAQs -->
  <div class="mb-6">
    <div class="text-center max-w-xl mx-auto mb-8">
      <h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white">
        Beginner Myth Busters
      </h3>
      <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-zinc-400 mt-1">
        Clearing up common misconceptions before your first sit.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-3 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      
      <div class="p-4 sm:p-5 rounded-2xl bg-white/[0.02] border border-white/[0.05]">
        <h4 class="text-sm font-semibold text-white mb-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="text-rose-400 font-bold">Myth:</span>
          <span>"I have to stop thinking completely to meditate."</span>
        </h4>
        <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed pl-6">
          <strong class="text-emerald-400">Reality:</strong> The human brain produces roughly 60,000 thoughts a day. Meditation is not about stopping thoughts; it's about learning not to chase them. Think of thoughts as clouds passing in the sky while you remain the observer.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-4 sm:p-5 rounded-2xl bg-white/[0.02] border border-white/[0.05]">
        <h4 class="text-sm font-semibold text-white mb-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="text-rose-400 font-bold">Myth:</span>
          <span>"I need to pay for an app with a talking guide."</span>
        </h4>
        <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed pl-6">
          <strong class="text-emerald-400">Reality:</strong> Guided talking voices can create dependency and cognitive listening fatigue. Simple unguided meditation with authentic acoustic bells trains your brain in genuine, self-directed emotional regulation.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-4 sm:p-5 rounded-2xl bg-white/[0.02] border border-white/[0.05]">
        <h4 class="text-sm font-semibold text-white mb-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="text-rose-400 font-bold">Myth:</span>
          <span>"If I feel fidgety or restless, I'm doing it wrong."</span>
        </h4>
        <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed pl-6">
          <strong class="text-emerald-400">Reality:</strong> Modern screens flood our brains with dopamine. When you first sit in silence, your nervous system naturally releases pent-up stimulation. Simply observe the fidgetiness with gentle curiosity—it dissolves within a few minutes.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>

</section>
